Produce a concise document title in {{.Language}}.

The source content may be in any language. The title MUST always be in {{.Language}}, regardless of the source language. The content was extracted by OCR and may contain errors — infer through them.

A GOOD title:
- 4 to 10 words, Title Case
- Identifies the correspondent (or key topic) + a specific descriptor + (optionally) a date or period
- Examples:
  - "Deutsche Telekom Internet Invoice — March 2024"
  - "Aufenthaltstitel Renewal Confirmation — 2024"
  - "Hotel Adlon Berlin Booking — 2024-05-12"
  - "Lufthansa Refund Receipt — LH4582"
  - "BVG Monthly Ticket Receipt — 2024-03"

A BAD title (never produce):
- Generic ("Invoice", "Document", "Letter", "Receipt")
- Wrapped in quotes
- Ends with a period
- Translates entity names that have no clean {{.Language}} equivalent (keep "Bundesamt für Migration und Flüchtlinge" as-is — do not Anglicize agency names)
- Contains only the document type with no specifics

If `<original_title>` is meaningful (not a filename like "scan_001.pdf"), treat it as a hint.

<original_title>{{.Title}}</original_title>
<content>
{{.Content}}
</content>

OUTPUT: only the title text, in {{.Language}}. No quotes, no trailing period, no commentary.
